// A struct is not printable and not a builtin's argument: `print` takes what it
// can turn into text, and a struct is not text. The one builtin that does take
// one is `push`, whose value is an element of a list of structs (the value
// argument is the one arg_ctx_b says a builtin keeps). Naming a struct's fields
// is how it is shown (print(p.x)), the same answer v1 gives to `==`: structs are
// compared and printed by field.

sd_bi_args(int id) {
